> The current behavior isn't too bad in 4.2

@akien-mga The current behaviour is borderline unusable. There is no indication that anything is saved after hitting CTRL+S, the only thing I'm seeing as a user is that the scene tab still has an unsaved asterisk behind its name. The script editor does not show anything like this, which _at the very least_ should be the case if this PR does not get merged. CTRL+S to save the script might make sense if the script editor was always fullscreen or in a separate window, but it is not. Even if people prefer that workflow, it shouldn't be forced and instead be implemented as an editor setting.

For me this is by far the most annoying bug (or bug-like behaviour) I have experienced in any version of Godot _including_ some of the early betas of Godot 4.0. I'd take a regular crash over things not saving any day.
